COMPILATION OF: E48D6

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E48D6

   1 a 0000 E48D6:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-48/P2d] STORE INTO a static CHARACTER (fixed): a two-
   4 a 0006      character literal stored into a three-character static cell
   5 a 0006      that already carries an initialiser.  My automatic route pools
   6 a 0006      the source literal (scratch s1 grew DATA 3 -> 5); does DR pool
   7 a 0006      again beside an already-initialised static cell, or copy into
   8 a 0006      it? */
   9 c 0006   dcl b bit(1) static initial('0'b);
  10 c 0006   dcl s char(3) static initial('AB');
  11 c 0006   s = 'CD';
  12 c 0013   put list('S=', s);
  13 c 0035   stop;
  14 a 0038 end E48D6;

CODE SIZE = 0038
DATA AREA = 0008
FREE SYMS = 38A1
END  COMPILATION
